# === QDL Self-Hosting Compiler (v0.1) ===
# This QDL script defines how to parse and execute QDL from within QDL (Phase 2: Self-Hosting)

# Note: This bootstrap logic assumes we are running in an already-functional QDL VM

:compile
# R0 = current line index
# R1 = total line count
# R2 = pointer to script buffer
# R3 = output memory address base
A 0 0         # line index = 0
R 1 line_count  # total lines
A 2 1000      # script buffer base address
A 3 2000      # bytecode output address

:loop
K 0 end_compile   # if R0 == line_count, end
R 4 1000          # R4 = current line token (assume pre-tokenized)
# Simplified: Copy token to output memory slot
Q 2000 4
B 3 1             # move output ptr forward
B 0 1             # move to next line
J loop

:end_compile
P

# === Bootstrap Driver (external Python loader still feeds script buffer) ===
# Once this logic is self-hosted, even the loader will be in QDL

:main
O compile        # call compiler
# Eventually call "run" here once bytecode compiled
H 9              # output done
